## Today's topics

- Making (better) tables

# Making (better) tables

## Package *gt*

![<https://gt.rstudio.com>](https://gt.rstudio.com/reference/figures/gt_parts_of_a_table.svg){#fig-parts-of-gt-table}

## *gt* tutorial

- Gather data
- Format it as a 'tibble', a special type of data frame

https://gt.rstudio.com/articles/gt.html

## Setup


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
library(gt)
library(dplyr)
library(tibble)
```
:::


## Gathering & formatting


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-line-numbers="|1|2-5|6"}
islands_tbl <-
  tibble(
    name = names(islands),
    size = islands
  ) |>
  slice_max(size, n = 10)
```
:::


## Inspecting


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
islands_tbl
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
# A tibble: 10 × 2
   name           size
   <chr>         <dbl>
 1 Asia          16988
 2 Africa        11506
 3 North America  9390
 4 South America  6795
 5 Antarctica     5500
 6 Europe         3745
 7 Australia      2968
 8 Greenland       840
 9 New Guinea      306
10 Borneo          280
```


:::
:::


## Display islands


::: {#tbl-islands-gt .cell output-location='slide'}

```{.r .cell-code}
# Create a display table showing ten of
# the largest islands in the world
gt_tbl <- gt(islands_tbl)

# Show the gt Table
gt_tbl
```

