## Selecting data

- Remember, we often want a continuous variable and one or more discrete (nominal or ordinal) variables


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
penquins_island_sex_mass <- penguins |>
  select(island, body_mass, sex)
```
:::


## Summarize


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-line-numbers="|1|2|3-7|8"}
penguins_tbl <- penquins_island_sex_mass |>
  group_by(sex) |>
  summarize(sample_n = n(),
            mean = mean(body_mass),
            median = median(body_mass),
            min = min(body_mass),
            max = max(body_mass)) |>
  gt()
```
:::


## Plot the table


::: {#tbl-penguins .cell tbl-cap='A summary table from the *penguins* dataset. Inspired by the *gt* package demo.' output-location='slide'}

